---
title: "Introduction to Computer Programming for Engineers"
code: "EGR-125"
category: "engineering"
credits: "4"
prerequisites:
  - "2026/MTH-162"
  - "2026/EGR-121"
corequisites:
  - "2026/MTH-162"
  - "2026/EGR-121"
prerequisiteNote: "Prerequisite: MTH 162; Corequisite: EGR 121"
corequisiteNote: "Prerequisite: MTH 162; Corequisite: EGR 121"
---

Introduces problem solving and implementation of computer software solutions using a high-level programming language in a structured environment. Includes concepts and practice of algorithm design, language syntax, control structures, arrays, and introduction to object-oriented programming. Covers engineering applications, such as mathematical modeling, file input and output, and basic numerical methods. The assignments in this course require mathematical problem-solving skills, algebraic modeling, and functions, and use of variables. Lecture 4 hours. Total 4 hours per week. Additional course fee applies.
